  "result": "Fixed. `Cart.remove` in `shop/models.py:32` compared the SKU you passed in against the item's **name** instead of its SKU:\n\n```python\nself.lines = [l for l in self.lines if l.item.name != sku]   # before\nself.lines = [l for l in self.lines if l.item.sku != sku]    # after\n```\n\nSo `remove('sku-1')` was checking against `'Widget'`, never matched, and removed nothing. `Cart.add` already matches lines by SKU, so `remove` now does the same.\n\n**Checks:**\n- `python3 -m shop.demo` now prints `1` (only the Gadget is left). Before the fix it printed `2`.\n- `python3 -m unittest`: all 6 tests pass. pytest isn't installed here, so I used unittest, and the tests are written for it anyway.\n\nNone of the existing tests call `Cart.remove`, which is how this slipped through. I can add a regression test to `tests/` if you'd like.",
